      "note_id": "loanwords_both_ways",
      "kind": "helpful_transfer",
      "text": "English and Korean are not related, so there are no look-alike cousins. These are loanwords that went in both directions. The first 10 are English words that came from Korean, mostly food and culture, so you may know them already; the Korean sounds a little different from how English says it. The last 8 are Korean words that came from English and are written in Hangul, bent to Korean sounds (there is no “f” or “z”, and extra vowels break up groups of consonants).",
      "pairs": [
